privateData.editorialMd:
Build differences

Start at the second number in `readings`. Subtract the number just before it from the current number. Repeat for each later number. Put the answers in order. For [5, 8, 2], `differences` is [3, -6]. A list with fewer than two numbers gives an empty `differences`.

Return the answer

Count the even numbers in `differences`. Store the count in `evenCount`. A number is even when it divides by 2 with no remainder. Complete `neighborNotesEvenKeyCensus` so it returns `evenCount`. Return it, do not print it.

Why this works

Each value in `differences` follows task 1. The later tasks use only those values. Keeping these steps separate helps avoid returning the list when the question asks for one number. Check empty input, one item, repeated values, and the largest allowed input.

Efficiency goal: time O(n); extra memory, including the helper list, O(n). n is the input length. These labels describe how work and memory grow with the input.

